@startuml Architecture_Overview
!theme plain
title Portfolio website — target architecture
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 60

node "Web Browser" {
    [JavaScript UI\nHTML, CSS, and page state] as UI
    [React project feed;\n incremental cards] as Feed
    [API Client\nfetch()] as Client
}

cloud "REST API over HTTP(S)\nJSON requests and responses" as Network

node "Backend Server (Node.js + Express)" {
    package "Presentation Layer" {
        [Static File Serving\npublic/] as Static
        [REST Routes & Middleware] as Routes
    }

    package "Business Layer" {
        [Services & Domain Rules\nAccounts, tokens, projects, CV,\nand feed interactions] as Services
    }

    package "Persistence Layer" {
        [PostgreSQL Access\nDatabase connection and SQL queries] as Persistence
    }
}

database "PostgreSQL\nAccounts, sessions, projects, profiles,\nand posts/likes/comments" as DB
folder "Server file storage\nProject media and builds" as Files

UI --> Client : invokes API
UI --> Feed : mount planned #/feed screen
Feed --> Client : cursor reads and session-bound interactions
Client --> Network : calls API
UI --> Static : loads pages and assets over HTTP(S)
Network --> Routes : api requests
Routes --> Services : validate and handle operations
Services --> Persistence : read and write records
Persistence --> DB
Services --> Files : resolve authorized existing media

note right of Client
  Sign-in uses a JWT access token
  in the Authorization header and a refresh
  token in an HttpOnly cookie.
end note

note right of Feed
  Public landing page.
  React owns only the feed container.
  Public reads filter published projects;
  likes/comments require an active session.
  No direct browser-to-database connection.
end note

@enduml
